# N-1 evidence: `type native "text" into "query"` — taps a native field to
# focus it, then types via `input text`, against the Android Settings
# search bar (another fully native surface, no Flutter widget tree).
#
# Tapping "Search settings" on the Settings home screen navigates to a
# dedicated search screen (a real Activity transition, not an in-place
# focus) — the same "wait after navigation" idiom this DSL already uses
# for Flutter screens applies here too, so the transition gets its own
# explicit wait before the type step runs against the now-stable screen.

test "type native focuses and types into a real native text field"
  tap native "Search settings"
  wait 2 seconds
  type native "wifi" into "Search settings"
  wait 2 seconds
